// scripts/pyrightconfig.json — brings the gate's own Python under the type checker that already covers
// app/ and tests/.
//
// The [tool.pyright] block in fl_backend/pyproject.toml declares include = ["app", "tests"], so it governs
// fl_backend/ and nothing else. Without this file the python here would be linted by ruff and type-checked
// by nobody, which is exactly the gap that block closes for app/ and tests/. These are the files the gate
// is BUILT from: a type error in check_scope.py is a gate that reports the wrong scope.
//
// No venvPath or venv, unlike the backend block, and that is not an omission: every import here is standard
// library or a sibling module in this folder. Pointing at fl_backend/.venv would make the gate's own tooling
// depend on the backend environment being installed, which is a dependency it does not otherwise have.
//
// typeCheckingMode matches the backend's "basic" for the reason stated there — "strict" demands an
// annotation on every local, which is a different project from "the editor and the gate agree".
//
// It lives HERE rather than at the repository root for the same reason scripts/ruff.toml does: a root config
// would become the nearest one for fl_backend/ as well, and override the include the backend has chosen.
// pythonVersion is PINNED because nothing here lets pyright infer it: with no venv declared it falls
// back to the interpreter it happens to find, which is 3.14 on the dev machine and older on the CI
// runner -- and the two then disagree about what parses. The caller cannot guarantee it either:
// scripts/_lib.sh :: any_python falls back to a bare python3 off PATH, so the pin is what states the
// version these scripts are written for.
{
  "include": ["."],
  "typeCheckingMode": "basic",
  "pythonVersion": "3.14"
}
